notes=("Kept all three old kinds (Teapot, Kyusu, Gaiwan). Old Teapot models Houhin and Shiboridashi moved into Kyusu types; old Kyusu models (ushirode, uwade, yokode) became types. "
 "Added Chagama (kama) as a kind from the Japanese tea utensils page. Left out: Gyokko kiln (pages 403), Kunzan and Hokujo (no source found), Wedgwood teapot archetype (no teapot-specific page), "
 "originator attributions for Yixing shapes (only retailer snippets), Royal Albert and Cauldon brand entries (no brand page retrieved). Cups (yunomi, gongfu cups) stay in Tableware.")
